      "writtenOn": "2020-06-01T22:44:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this function would be clearer by using a local variable to set the maximum speed supported by the USB/TBT cable, and reflowing to a single exit point with a check against board_get_max_tbt_speed().\n\nThe common exit point would look like:\n    \n    /* Logic to set usb4_cable_speed based on passive, REV30, TBT checks\n       as before */\n\n    if (usb4_cable_speed \u003e board_get_max_usb_speed(port))\n        usb4_cable_speed \u003d board_get_max_usb_speed(port);\n\n    return usb4_cable_speed;\n\nboard_get_max_usb_speed() is optional - this just converts board_get_max_tbt_speed() to enum usb_rev_ss.",
